==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|aazaan}}, {{l|en|azan}}, {{l|en|athan}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|أَذَان}}. {{root|en|ar|ء ذ ن}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɑːˈðɑːn/|/əˈðɑːn/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːn|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q165494}} {{lb|en|Islam}} The [[call to prayer]], which consisted originally of simply four [[takbir]]s followed by the statement {{l|ar||لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا ٱلله}} {{l|ar||(أَشْهَدُ أَنْ)}}.
#: {{ux|en|If one pray alone, then no '''adhan''' is needed.}}

